      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HARRO HILL (6) settled in the leading division the went to the front and finished too well to win for the second time in a row last start over 1800m at this track, getting there by 1.75 metres. This doesn't look as hard so she is sure to prove tough to beat. KETO NZ (5) has had two runs this prep and is yet to finish in the top three. Was again unable to find the frame last time when he finished ninth over 2270m at Riverina Paceway, beaten 50 metres. Has the ability to take care of this field. STAR MAN (4) is worth plenty of thought off a last-start win by a head at this track over 1800m. STYLISTIK (3) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and finished eighth last start over 1800m at this track, coming home 25 metres from the winner. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Has the talent to make his presence felt.",
